"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".presented"},{"type":"text","text":" — useful for anything more specific than “was this a pop”, like varying copy or analytics by referrer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["if source.originatingScreen == .home {","    \/\/ came straight from the home screen","}"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}],"title":"ScreenStateStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holder of a screen’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference"},{"text":", driving both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI and UIKit consumers from a single source of truth.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateStore"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenState","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenState"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"showing data, or failed.","type":"text"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates"